    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n71033" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νοσ-ερός</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ά</span>,
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όν</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νοσηρός</span>
			, of symptoms, <i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Aph.</u>
				7.67
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ν. κῶλον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Or.</u>
					1016
				</span></i>
			 (anap.); <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ν. κοίτα</span> a bed
				<i>of sickness,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Hipp.</u>
				131
			</span></i> (lyr.), cf. <i><span class="en">
				179
			</span></i> (anap.); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ν. χειμών</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>Pr.</u>
					861b22
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νοσερά,</span> opp. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑγιεινά,</span> Polystr.<i><span class="en">
				p.3
			</span></i> W., cf. <i><span class="en">
				Alex.Aphr.
				<u>in Top.</u>
				71.2
			</span></i>; <i>unhealthy,</i> of persons, <i><span class="en">
				Ph.
				1.198
			</span></i> (
				Sup.
			). Adv.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ρῶς, ἔχειν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>Pol.</u>
					1320b36
				</span></i>
			.</div>
